,"fullName":"TC-01 Patient Chart Card › TC-01/S04"},"descriptionHtml":"<div class=\"rc-approach\"><p><b>Approach</b> · TC-01 Patient Chart Card · <b>S04</b> Each badge class shows on the card: New Admission, Consult, Follow-up, both contexts</p><p><b>UAT steps / ticket ACs covered:</b></p><ul><li><b>U4</b> The card shows the New Admission / Follow-up / Consult badge. (UAT TC-01; TFA-92579 AC 3)</li></ul><p><b>Test design technique: </b>Equivalence classes (equivalence) — Check the same rule again with another class of input (Hospital / Nursing Home, other data); every class has to be right.</p><p><b>Given </b>Standard fixture</p><p><b>When </b>In the chart header set Admission status to New Admission, go back to the list; repeat for Consult and Follow-up; then the same for the resident in Nursing Home</p><p><b>Then </b>After each change the list card shows exactly the chosen badge and not the other two</p><p><b>Pass rule (oracle, excerpt): </b>oracle.mjs on the list page (no other badge words there): mustContain 'Open chart for &lt;name&gt;' and the chosen badge, mustNotContain the other two. One patient per context, so not evidence for U8; the badge roll is S07</p><p><b>Where it ran: </b>dev unit U21; test method AGENT · Browser agent; lane planned in the matrix: browser agent (automated)</p><p><small>S04 is our own case number (its number in the coverage matrix cases/TC-01.matrix.json), not a step number of the UAT document.</small></p></div><p><b>Environment: dev</b> — dev deployment, build <code>e02167f</code> (Deploy Convex, 2026-10-12T18:24:27Z); account and address are not written into the report; run folder <code>runs/2026-10-14-dev</code>.</p><p><b>Test method:</b> AGENT · Browser agent; secondary: PW · Playwright script — as classified in cases/test-methods.json, which says it runs on both; Source: <code>dev</code>.</p><p><b>UAT item:</b> TC-01 Patient Chart Card · <b>Section:</b> A1 · Home Screen &amp; Dashboard · <b>Scenario:</b> TC-01/S04</p><p><b>Each 